  "narrative": "The second discovery panel is mixed but contains one very clear signal and two near-threshold signals. The strongest result is for feature_002: H41 was claimed in the negative direction, but R23 is signed negative throughout, meaning the raw exposed-minus-comparator effect is positive by about 0.8315 units, with signed magnitude and interval excluding the threshold in the opposite direction. I therefore reject H41 as stated, because it was the wrong direction, but this is strong evidence for a reversed, scientifically meaningful association of feature_002=1 with higher/less-negative outcome_001. I propose a linked reversed claim for feature_002 with direction +1 and initial assessment accept based on R23; this remains a dataset-specific association, not causal evidence. H39 is the best positive-direction candidate: feature_003=1 versus 0 has signed effect +0.1409 with interval [0.0616, 0.2202], i.e. raw effect about -0.1409 in the claimed stronger-dependency direction. The point estimate is slightly below the 0.15 threshold but the interval crosses it and excludes zero, so it is unresolved and worth independent validation. I request validation only for H39; I do not validate the near-null interaction or main effects. H23 is also in the claimed direction with signed effect +0.1066 and interval [0.0351, 0.1782], but it is weaker than H39, so I defer it. All other valid second-panel estimates are either too small, opposite but below threshold, or null, including marker-marker interactions, discrete severity contrast, and high-log-PFS interactions. Follow-up proposals test robustness and confounding of the new feature_002 and feature_003 signals: feature_003 within feature_002=0, feature_002 within feature_003=0, and feature_002 effect modification by high log-PFS.",
  "research_notes": "Current conclusions: no currently accepted first-panel claims; H4-H8 and H10-H12 remain null and closed. Second panel: H41 was tested in wrong direction; reversed feature_002 main effect is proposed with initial accept based on R23 and should be treated as the main discovery candidate. H39 is the only near-threshold claim in its claimed direction and is now active for independent validation. H23 is a weaker near-threshold claim and is deferred. All other new valid second-panel comparisons are rejected/closed. Follow-up priorities: validate H39; then run/evaluate the linked feature_002/feature_003 conditional analyses and feature_002 high-log-PFS interaction if they provide new sample. Interpret all results as associations in this supplied dataset; do not infer causality or generalizability. Continue to avoid exact continuous exposure contrasts; use binary/categorical contrasts or numeric thresholds in eligibility/subgroup fields.",
